Clear the Android BCB in `misc` at boot so the next reset leaves recovery.

The chosen loop is: `boot` = TWRP (adb control plane), `recovery` = the iOS
boot image.  ABL's `boot-recovery` BCB is only cleared by a successful Android
boot, which iOS never does, so after a `fastboot flash recovery` +
`fastboot reboot recovery` the device would keep booting recovery - the loop
could not close.  This patch zeros the first 4096 bytes of the `misc`
partition (the Android bootloader_message area: 2048-byte message + spare),
very early in the eMMC root init, with the driver's raw writer:

  - the `misc` partition is located by name with the existing GPT parser in
    onc_emmc.c (new `misc` match recorded in `oe.misc_lba/misc_nblocks`);
  - 8 x 512-byte zero blocks are written with oe_write_lba() under
    onc_emmc_lock, right after the partition table is parsed;
  - boot arg `sweetclearmisc=0` disables it (default ON; clearing an
    already-clear BCB is harmless and the loop depends on it);
  - banner: `SWEET MISC: cleared BCB at block 0x...` (or a skip reason).

It runs only when the card is writable (emmcroot_orw=1) and `misc` exists and
is large enough; no other partition is touched.  If `misc` is not found the
banner says so and nothing is written.

Note: this clears the BCB *during* the iOS boot, i.e. the current boot already
happened; the NEXT reset boots TWRP - which is exactly the intended order.

Only bsd/dev/onc_emmc.c changes; base is the post-0132 content.
